# Build context for docsgpt/Dockerfile is the repository root, so the image can
# carry the `application` import alias next to the `docsgpt` package. Allow only
# what the image needs; everything else (docs, tests, venvs) stays out.
*
!docsgpt/
# Only the alias file: an upgraded checkout may still hold gitignored
# application/{inputs,indexes,vectors,.env} from the old layout.
!application/__init__.py
# The web UI's source and the script that builds it (the `ui` stage).
!frontend/
!scripts/build_frontend.sh

# Inside the package: caches, local runtime data and secrets never ship.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
docsgpt/.pytest_cache/
docsgpt/.ruff_cache/
docsgpt/.coverage
docsgpt/htmlcov/
docsgpt/*.log
docsgpt/indexes/
docsgpt/inputs/
docsgpt/vectors/
docsgpt/*.faiss
docsgpt/*.pkl
docsgpt/.env
docsgpt/.env.*
docsgpt/Dockerfile
# A local UI build stays out: the `ui` stage builds the one the image serves.
docsgpt/static/

# Inside the frontend: installed packages and local builds are redone in the
# `ui` stage, and local VITE_* overrides must not be baked into a published image.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.env.local
frontend/.env.*.local
frontend/*.log
# The frontend image's own build files; changing them must not rebuild this UI.
frontend/Dockerfile
frontend/.dockerignore
frontend/docker/
